  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "👁️ Lash Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a lash tech, lash studio or lash and brow bar."
    },
    "intro": "A good lash business name is soft, short and easy to fit in an Instagram handle, with a hint of what you do: classic, volume or lash and brow. The **Lash Business Name Generator** suggests names for a lash tech, lash studio, eyelash extension business or lash and brow bar. Pick catchy, cute, modern, luxury or aesthetic, or make a lash business name with your name or your town.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good lash business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Built to Lash</strong>: a pun on built to last.</li><li><strong>Lash Things First</strong>: a pun on first things first.</li><li><strong>Volume Control</strong>: a joke on volume lashes.</li><li><strong>Flutter By Lashes</strong>: a soft pun on butterfly.</li><li><strong>Fawn Lash Co.</strong>: cute, and fawns are famous for their lashes.</li><li><strong>Plume</strong>: one modern word that suggests feathery lashes.</li><li><strong>Clin d'Œil Lashes</strong>: luxury French: <em>clin d'œil</em> means a wink.</li><li><strong>The Thistle Lash Room</strong>: aesthetic, with a Scottish touch.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How lash business names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Lash words tell clients what you offer.</strong> <em>Classic</em> lashes are one extension per natural lash, <em>volume</em> lashes are a fan of several fine extensions on each, and <em>hybrid</em> mixes the two. Words like volume, wisp and flutter fit straight into names.</li><li><strong>Puns on \"lash\"</strong> are popular (<em>Lash Forward</em>, <em>The Lash Word</em>), so check yours isn't already used nearby.</li><li><strong>Lash and brow</strong> is a common ending if you do both.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>A name from a generator is a starting point, not permission to use it. Before you order the sign, the boxes or the van livery:</p><ul><li><strong>Company register.</strong> In the UK, search Companies House; you can't register a limited company with the same name as an existing one. In the US, search your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Trade marks.</strong> Search the UK trade mark register (or the USPTO in the US) for the goods and services you'll sell.</li><li><strong>Domain and handles.</strong> Check the .co.uk or .com and the Instagram and TikTok handles you'll need.</li><li><strong>Your area.</strong> Search a map app for businesses with the same or a similar name nearby.</li></ul><p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or use the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to run most of these at once. For the full process, read our guide, <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>. This is general guidance, not legal advice.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Making the name work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Keep it short for the handle.</strong> Lash techs are found on Instagram, so the handle is the real name.</li><li><strong>Think about growth.</strong> Your own name builds a following; a brand name is easier to grow into a studio with staff.</li></ul><p>Offering more treatments? Try the <a href=\"beauty-salon-name-generator.html\">Beauty Salon</a>, <a href=\"nail-salon-name-generator.html\">Nail Salon</a> and <a href=\"hair-salon-name-generator.html\">Hair Salon</a> name generators.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_beauty-names.html\">beauty and wellness business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good lash business names?",
        "answer": "Soft, short names that fit an Instagram handle: puns like Built to Lash or Flutter By Lashes, cute names like Fawn Lash Co., or French luxury like Clin d'Œil Lashes, which means a wink."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I check a lash business name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, also search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as another salon nearby with a similar name can confuse clients."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should my lash business name mention brows too?",
        "answer": "If you offer brow lamination, tinting or shaping as well as lashes, saying so helps clients searching for both: \"Lash & Brow Studio\" is a common, clear ending. If lashes are all you do, or you might add other treatments later, a name such as \"Flutter Lash Co.\" keeps it simple, and you can list brows on your menu."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's the difference between classic and volume lashes?",
        "answer": "Classic lashes are one extension on each natural lash; volume lashes are a fan of several finer extensions on each one. Hybrid lashes mix the two."
      }
    ]
  }
}
